# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# Without this, line-ending behaviour is per-machine: this checkout had
# core.autocrlf=true, which writes CRLF into the working copy, while a macOS or
# Linux checkout typically does not. Either way a contributor can commit CRLF
# into the repository and turn a one-line change into a whole-file diff.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect text, and `eol=lf` pins the stored form to LF so
# every machine produces identical bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never line-ending-translate these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# Signing and keystore material must survive byte-for-byte.
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
*.p8 binary
*.p12 binary
*.mobileprovision binary